INT. QUICKROUTE DELIVERY WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

Cavernous. Steel shelving rises into dark. Pallets stacked like gravestones. A single forklift beeps somewhere unseen.

ANGLE ON a loading bay: Teo Marchetti, 40s, broad shoulders, a scar through one eyebrow, scans a package. Beside him, Alex Rowan, 17, they/them, oversized hi-vis vest, drags a box twice their size.

TEO
Easy. Lift with your legs.

ALEX
I am lifting with my legs, Dad.

Teo hides a smile.

A voice crackles over the PA.

KEIKO (V.O.)
Teo, we've got a rush on bay six. Insurance audit tomorrow, so don't lose anything.

Keiko Tanaka, 50s, floor manager, appears at the end of the aisle with a clipboard, gray hair under a hairnet.

INSERT - THE PACKAGE LABEL

"HANDLE WITH CARE. FRAGILE. THIS SIDE UP."

Alex's box slips. It hits the concrete. Something inside cracks.

Everyone freezes.

TEO
(low)
Alex.

ALEX
(small)
It was heavy.

WE SEE Keiko's face harden, then soften.

KEIKO
(to Teo)
Take the night off. Both of you.

BACK TO SCENE

Teo kneels, lifts the box, shakes it gently. A rattle. A sigh.

TEO
(to Alex, soft)
Hey. Nobody's fired. It's a lamp. We'll buy the lamp.

Alex wipes their eyes with a glove. Teo ruffles their hair. The forklift beeps on.
